From 353961e52b991936a8bf6897c43c654308f608e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:17:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(state): review follow-ups for the holder-window and
 doctor changes

- A new episode a peer started (its record begins after this handle last
  saw a holder) no longer inherits this handle's old window.
- Doctor advice is coherent when only non-gateway processes hold state.db,
  and two gateways are told they block each other.
- Holder descriptions elide inline source only for a Python interpreter's
  -c (gateway.status_inline_source), never a shell's or a script's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hermes_cli/doctor_state.py                    | 23 ++++++++---
 hermes_state_holders.py                       | 10 +++--
 hermes_state_schema.py                        |  9 +++--
 .../test_doctor_fts_deferral_holders.py       | 35 ++++++++++++++++-
 .../test_fts_futile_holder_churn.py           | 39 +++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 102 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hermes_cli/doctor_state.py b/hermes_cli/doctor_state.py
